# ===========================================================================
# GeoHam — Multi-Scale Symplectic Change Detector
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#  [R1] FRAMING FIX: Removed all "physics-grounded" claims. Integration is
#       explicitly framed as "symplectic-regularised feature evolution" —
#       a structured numerical scheme applied to learned dynamics. There is
#       no physical PDE residual being enforced (not a PINN).
#
#  [R2] MULTI-SCALE INTEGRATION: Störmer-Verlet now runs at 3 FPN levels
#       (64×64, 32×32, 16×16) with shared weights, NOT only at the bottleneck.
#       Fine boundary detail is preserved via divergences at 64×64 and a raw
#       absolute-difference skip at 128×128 that bypasses integration entirely.
#
#  [R3] SIMPLIFIED LOSS: 3-term TopologicalPersistenceLoss with hardcoded
#       Morse-theory weights (0.5, 0.3) replaced by a single BoundaryAwareLoss
#       term based on morphological gradient of the GT mask. One term, one
#       hyper-parameter (λ_bnd), ablatable in a single row.
#
# Architecture:
#   EfficientNet-B2 (shared)
#     → 4 FPN scales  [C0 128px | C1 64px | C2 32px | C3 16px]
#     → MultiScaleSymplecticIntegrator (shared weights, proj_dim=64)
#         div_1 [64px], div_2 [32px], div_3 [16px]
#     + raw abs-diff skip_0  [128px, no integration]
#     → FPNFusionDecoder  (coarse→fine)
#     → Logits [256px]
#
# Compared to V1:
#   · Integrator parameter count ↓  (352-dim → 64-dim shared)
#   · Forward FLOPs ≈ same (3 small integrations vs 1 large)
#   · Feature richness ↑  (3 divergence scales + 1 raw skip)
#   · Loss terms  3 → 2  (focal-dice + boundary)
#   · Energy conservation renamed → symplectic regularisation
# ===========================================================================

